future amounts to a single present value amount based upon market expectations (including present value techniques, option pricing, and excess earnings models).","context":"●Cost approach: Amount that would be required to replace the service capacity of an asset (replacement cost).","section":"Segment Reporting","block":706,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-032111","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-19","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000839470","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/839470/000110465926032111/wwr-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/372cfc2ccce403f527807f5bf9edfd280ae9a858d5bbd6e2dfbd797c46f22019.bin","sha256":"372cfc2ccce403f527807f5bf9edfd280ae9a858d5bbd6e2dfbd797c46f22019"}},{"id":"988018224d0dbec4b4651f8889a39d54efd35ab78a36708667c781e0361ce33d","quote":"The Company considers all highly liquid instruments purchased with an original maturity of three months or less to be cash equivalents. The Company continually monitors its positions with, and the credit quality of, the financial institutions with which it invests. Periodically throughout the year, the Company has maintained balances in various U.S. operating accounts in excess of U.S. federally insured limits.","context":"●Income approach: Techniques to convert future amounts to a single present value amount based upon market expectations (including present value techniques, option pricing, and excess earnings models).","section":"Segment Reporting","block":707,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-032111","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-19","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000839470","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/839470/000110465926032111/wwr-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/372cfc2ccce403f527807f5bf9edfd280ae9a858d5bbd6e2dfbd797c46f22019.bin","sha256":"372cfc2ccce403f527807f5bf9edfd280ae9a858d5bbd6e2dfbd797c46f22019"}},{"id":"67bda586987d5fb680b865fd3a2843927bc95ef4432bbadeafdf7062b0eb131a","quote":"Stock-based compensation awards consist of stock options, RSU’s and bonus shares issued under the Company’s equity incentive plans, which include the 2013 Plan and the Inducement Plan.","context":"Stock-Based Compensation Accounting","section":"Segment Reporting","block":709,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-032111","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-19","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000839470","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/839470/000110465926032111/wwr-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/372cfc2ccce403f527807f5bf9edfd280ae9a858d5bbd6e2dfbd797c46f22019.bin","sha256":"372cfc2ccce403f527807f5bf9edfd280ae9a858d5bbd6e2dfbd797c46f22019"}},{"id":"a23c0bd117f64db13cf3256b5d28370503bf28b2c95f215a3324fb6bfe9c84c9","quote":"Compensation expense for all share-based compensation awards requires measurement at estimated fair value on the grant date. Compensation cost is recognized on a straight-line basis over the service vesting period, which represents the requisite service period. RSUs are valued at the fair value of the award on the date of grant, or using an advanced option-pricing model, such as a lattice model. Stock options are valued using the Black-Scholes option pricing model on the date of grant. The Company accounts for forfeitures upon occurrence and forfeited awards are available again for issuance under the 2013 Plan.","context":"Stock-based compensation awards consist of stock options, RSU’s and bonus shares issued under the Company’s equity incentive plans, which include the 2013 Plan and the Inducement Plan.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":710,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"